WEBVTT

00:11.020 --> 00:14.760
I'm, um, really sorry about the pamphlet.

00:14.760 --> 00:17.700
Why? You don't need to apologize.

00:17.700 --> 00:19.040
Yeah, but...

00:19.040 --> 00:22.660
It's fine. I don't want you to lie
 just to agree with me.

00:25.650 --> 00:28.340
I've been thinking recently.

00:28.730 --> 00:33.300
Ryuto, you know, Maria might be 
a better match for you than I am.

00:33.560 --> 00:34.400
Huh?

00:34.400 --> 00:38.360
You're both smart, you both agreed 
on the design for the pamphlet,

00:38.360 --> 00:40.280
and about those game streams or whatever?

00:40.280 --> 00:43.530
You have a lot more in common 
with Maria than me.

00:43.530 --> 00:44.570
What are you talking—

00:44.570 --> 00:46.020
At first, Ryuto,

00:46.020 --> 00:51.030
I thought you were interesting 
because you were so different from me.

00:51.580 --> 00:53.760
But as I started liking you more,

00:53.760 --> 00:57.990
it became obvious that we're 
completely different types of people.

00:57.990 --> 00:58.830
Come on...

00:58.830 --> 01:03.370
You'll probably get tired of me 
soon, anyway. I am a gyaru.

01:04.040 --> 01:08.580
The places we want to go and the things
we want to do are probably nothing alike.

01:10.020 --> 01:13.920
You might be happier 
dating Maria instead, Ryuto.

01:13.920 --> 01:14.980
Huh?

01:15.400 --> 01:18.940
You were on the roof 
with Maria during Sports Day, right?

01:18.940 --> 01:19.920
That's because—

01:19.920 --> 01:26.350
I know. You're too nice, 
and you didn't want to leave her alone.

01:27.330 --> 01:28.940
Pretty weird, right?

01:29.320 --> 01:33.610
I'm the one who wanted you 
to be kind to her. To be her friend.

01:33.610 --> 01:35.900
I'm the one who said all that.

01:36.220 --> 01:41.580
I just want to like you. 
There doesn't have to be any more to it.

01:42.200 --> 01:44.970
So why did I start feeling like this?

01:45.860 --> 01:51.170
I'm sorry. Since it's Maria, 
I can't just let it go.

01:51.480 --> 01:52.920
Runa, I really—

01:52.920 --> 01:53.960
Is this okay?

01:53.960 --> 01:54.710
Huh?

01:55.440 --> 01:59.090
Is it okay for us to keep dating like this?

02:01.040 --> 02:01.960
Listen, I really—

02:01.960 --> 02:03.930
I won't try to text you for a while.

02:05.020 --> 02:06.100
Runa!

02:09.900 --> 02:11.860
<i>I thought I couldn't catch her.</i>

02:13.000 --> 02:16.470
<i>If I did, what would I even say?</i>

02:17.140 --> 02:18.700
<i>I didn't know.</i>

02:20.880 --> 02:25.040
And today was our four-month anniversary.

02:31.920 --> 02:36.670
<b>Our Different Story:</b>

02:32.440 --> 02:36.670
<b>The Experienced You and the</b>

02:32.940 --> 02:36.670
<b>Inexperienced Me Go Different Ways.</b>

02:37.040 --> 02:38.760
You're so stupid.

02:39.080 --> 02:42.540
You should have just lied 
and taken Runa's side instead.

02:43.960 --> 02:45.060
I think...

02:47.080 --> 02:51.140
if I actually had to carry one around, 
I'd prefer the monochrome version.

02:58.040 --> 02:58.970
Runa...

03:01.410 --> 03:02.570
It's done!

03:03.990 --> 03:05.530
Chii-chan is so cute!

03:07.320 --> 03:08.790
Give it.

03:08.790 --> 03:09.870
Hmm?

03:09.870 --> 03:11.630
It's mine. Give it back.

03:11.630 --> 03:17.050
Huh? But you said you didn't 
want it anymore. That's why I took it.

03:17.050 --> 03:20.260
But they bought it for me.

03:20.260 --> 03:21.630
Still...

03:21.630 --> 03:22.930
Give it back!

03:30.560 --> 03:34.400
All right. Take good care 
of it this time, okay?

03:42.280 --> 03:45.770
Runa, you were always like that.

03:46.300 --> 03:51.020
Such a nice girl. Gentle, thoughtful.

03:51.880 --> 03:55.750
So I was actually really happy for you.

03:57.400 --> 04:02.840
Runa... I want you to be happy 
with Kashima-kun.

04:03.490 --> 04:05.980
But what am I supposed to do?

04:06.640 --> 04:08.820
I still feel this way.

04:11.260 --> 04:12.560
Oh, this looks great.

04:12.960 --> 04:14.730
Very well done.

04:14.730 --> 04:16.590
I can tell you worked hard on it.

04:16.590 --> 04:18.400
Thank you very much.

04:18.400 --> 04:20.090
I guess once you all settled on a cover,

04:20.090 --> 04:22.780
you were able to communicate 
with each other better.

04:22.780 --> 04:24.720
Well, yes.

04:24.720 --> 04:27.080
<i>Actually, we barely talked to each other</i>

04:27.080 --> 04:30.240
<i>and just pushed the work 
along like an assembly line.</i>

04:30.240 --> 04:34.190
So it looks like your work for 
the pamphlet committee is finished.

04:34.190 --> 04:35.600
Good job.

04:35.600 --> 04:36.460
Thank you.

04:37.210 --> 04:41.670
Staff Room

04:37.830 --> 04:41.670
I should probably tell them both 
that the pamphlet was okayed.

04:42.090 --> 04:45.010
I can tell Kurose-san at prep school and...

04:45.010 --> 04:46.970
<b>Good night</b>

04:47.340 --> 04:51.080
Yes, it is. What? Do you mean now?

04:51.560 --> 04:54.020
Should we meet in Ikebukuro?

04:54.330 --> 04:56.600
<i>Why is Runa speaking so politely?</i>

04:55.060 --> 04:56.600
Yes, that's all right.

04:56.990 --> 04:58.460
<i>Is it someone older?</i>

04:58.460 --> 05:00.670
All right. I'll go there immediately.

05:01.560 --> 05:03.450
Ru... Shirakawa-san!

05:04.380 --> 05:07.000
<i>Who was it? Was it a guy? A girl?</i>

05:07.960 --> 05:10.580
<i>I can't even think straight right now.</i>

05:10.960 --> 05:14.710
I really am such a wuss. Ugh.

05:16.680 --> 05:20.520
<i>Yamana-san. I bet she knows 
what happened between us.</i>

05:20.520 --> 05:23.340
<i>Maybe she knows who was on the phone, too.</i>

05:23.760 --> 05:25.120
You know, a guy like you...

05:25.120 --> 05:26.300
Y-Yes?!

05:27.240 --> 05:31.300
Um, well... I'm s-sorry!

05:34.280 --> 05:38.300
I thought you'd be able to make Runa happy.

05:38.730 --> 05:40.600
Not hurt her and stuff.

05:41.180 --> 05:42.470
Yamana-san...

05:42.950 --> 05:44.710
But it was useless.

05:46.030 --> 05:50.470
You know, love isn't all just fun and games.

05:50.870 --> 05:53.240
Seriously. What a letdown.

05:57.680 --> 05:59.480
Kashima-kun!

06:01.030 --> 06:02.420
Tanikita-san?

06:03.170 --> 06:05.260
I'm so glad I ran into you!

06:05.740 --> 06:07.960
Runachi isn't with you, is she?

06:07.960 --> 06:09.340
Uh, no.

06:09.870 --> 06:12.900
I want to talk to you about something. 
Is that okay?

06:15.820 --> 06:19.520
So I mean, I don't want you 
to freak out about it,

06:19.920 --> 06:22.980
but Runachi might have a sugar daddy.

06:24.010 --> 06:24.690
Su—

06:24.690 --> 06:26.650
A sugar daddy?!

06:26.650 --> 06:29.130
Th-That's like that thing, right?

06:29.130 --> 06:34.250
When a young girl goes on dates with 
an older guy and gets money for it?

06:34.250 --> 06:38.460
Yeah. And I saw them.

06:38.460 --> 06:42.300
I went to Ikebukuro to buy some merch.

06:41.080 --> 06:45.710
<b>Comedy</b>

06:41.080 --> 06:45.710
<b>Video Shop</b>

06:45.710 --> 06:49.210
Yeees! I got the new Lee Joon merch!

06:50.470 --> 06:52.640
<b>Sauce
Tonkatsu</b>

06:50.840 --> 06:52.640
<b>With Our Famous Sweet and Sour Sauce</b>

06:52.640 --> 06:54.220
Runachi?

06:57.180 --> 06:58.810
Huh?!

06:59.160 --> 07:02.520
He was about as tall as Jungwoo,
 and pretty hot.

07:02.520 --> 07:04.830
Could it have been this guy?

07:05.660 --> 07:07.690
No, someone else.

07:08.010 --> 07:10.040
He was younger.

07:10.040 --> 07:11.910
Maybe a college student.

07:11.910 --> 07:16.490
Is a college student "daddy" enough 
to be a sugar daddy, though?

07:16.490 --> 07:19.760
I don't know. Maybe, if he has enough money.

07:19.760 --> 07:23.130
I mean, if he didn't, how could he afford to 
pay tribute with such an expensive bag?

07:23.130 --> 07:24.940
Pay tribute?

07:26.090 --> 07:30.670
Tanikita-san, do you really think Runa's 
the kind of girl to have a sugar daddy?

07:30.670 --> 07:32.020
I don't know.

07:32.550 --> 07:37.960
Runachi is super nice, but she does 
have a kind of reckless side.

07:37.960 --> 07:40.760
Like, if someone gets pushy, she can't say no.

07:41.420 --> 07:42.860
Also,

07:43.230 --> 07:47.690
I heard from Nicole that things aren't 
great between you guys right now.

07:49.590 --> 07:51.900
It might just be my misunderstanding,

07:52.270 --> 07:57.210
but if she's feeling insecure over this 
and decided to do something risky...

07:57.210 --> 08:01.240
When I thought of that, I got worried 
and had to tell you.

08:02.570 --> 08:03.590
All right.

08:05.170 --> 08:07.630
Thanks for your concern.

08:07.630 --> 08:10.590
Kashima-kun, so what about Runachi?

08:10.910 --> 08:14.260
Don't worry. I trust Runa.

08:14.790 --> 08:17.430
If anything happens, then...

08:20.430 --> 08:22.820
it would all be my fault.

08:36.040 --> 08:39.180
<i>Oh, Yamada? Hey. What's up?</i>

08:39.180 --> 08:43.180
Actually, I have a favor to ask, Sekiya-san.

08:49.000 --> 08:50.380
Come in!

08:49.000 --> 08:51.460
<i>Seirin Festival</i>

08:49.000 --> 08:51.460
Haunted
House

08:49.960 --> 08:51.460
<i>Planetarium</i>

08:50.380 --> 08:52.490
Class 3 is running a haunted house!

08:52.490 --> 08:53.970
Would you like some of these?

08:53.970 --> 08:55.240
Thank you!

08:55.240 --> 08:56.430
Come on in!

08:58.390 --> 08:59.620
<b><i>Our Famous 
Curry Rice</i></b>

08:59.140 --> 09:01.040
Hey, that guy is so cool!

09:01.040 --> 09:03.480
I know! Maybe he's a graduate.

09:03.480 --> 09:07.050
Sekiya-san, don't you think 
you stick out a little?

09:07.440 --> 09:10.660
The same uniforms? Are you serious?

09:10.660 --> 09:11.790
Sekiya-san!

09:11.790 --> 09:13.780
Uh, yeah? What?

09:13.780 --> 09:17.950
Please pull it together. 
Why are you acting so strange?

09:17.950 --> 09:18.940
It's nothing.

09:20.730 --> 09:24.920
Okay, I know. I'll carry out the mission.

09:24.920 --> 09:28.830
I just have to uncover the identity 
of the sugar daddy, right?

09:28.830 --> 09:31.630
But you can't use the words "sugar daddy."

09:31.630 --> 09:34.520
We don't really know 
if that's the situation yet.

09:34.520 --> 09:37.300
Honestly, I can't see her 
doing that in the first place.

09:37.300 --> 09:40.200
Then why don't you just ask her directly?

09:40.200 --> 09:43.480
Like, "Who is the guy you were 
walking with in Ikebukuro?"

09:43.480 --> 09:47.020
If I could do that, I never would have 
asked someone like you for help.

09:47.020 --> 09:49.110
Someone like me? What?

09:53.620 --> 09:54.860
Tanikita-san?

09:54.860 --> 09:56.650
K...Kashima-kun!

09:56.650 --> 09:58.960
It's him! This is the guy!

09:58.960 --> 10:00.740
He's the guy who was walking with Runachi!

10:00.740 --> 10:02.040
Huh?

10:02.680 --> 10:03.420
What?

10:04.290 --> 10:06.090
Sekiya-san?

10:06.090 --> 10:06.870
Huh?

10:07.540 --> 10:11.250
<b>Pictures OK</b>

10:07.540 --> 10:11.250
<b><b>Maid Café</b></b>

10:07.920 --> 10:11.250
Wait. You mean your girlfriend 
is Shirakawa Runa?

10:12.960 --> 10:15.630
<i>I knew she didn't have a sugar daddy!</i>

10:15.630 --> 10:17.920
<i>But then that means...</i>

10:17.920 --> 10:20.890
<i>he's one of her exes?!</i>

10:20.890 --> 10:22.850
<b>Maid Café</b>

10:22.850 --> 10:27.810
<b>Maid Café</b>

10:23.280 --> 10:26.120
Sekiya-san, how could you do this to me?

10:26.120 --> 10:27.810
Now hold on a second.

10:28.120 --> 10:31.640
I never wanted to meet 
any of Runa's exes. Ever.

10:31.640 --> 10:33.650
I knew it would only fill me with hate.

10:33.950 --> 10:37.260
But then it had to be a filthy 
deviant like you, Sekiya-san?

10:37.260 --> 10:40.360
Hey! I'm telling you, you got it all wrong!

10:40.670 --> 10:43.330
Wait, "filthy deviant"? What the hell, man?

10:43.330 --> 10:47.290
<b>Maid Café</b>

10:43.600 --> 10:45.840
Well, you are, aren't you?

10:45.840 --> 10:47.290
Listen to me.

10:47.290 --> 10:52.000
Shirakawa Runa isn't my ex-girlfriend. 
She's my ex-girlfriend's friend.

10:52.000 --> 10:52.740
Huh?

10:53.340 --> 10:55.210
Here you are!

10:55.210 --> 11:00.440
One grape soda full of love and one 
emotion-infused special cappuccino.

10:55.210 --> 11:01.180
<b>Maid</b>

11:01.180 --> 11:06.140
If you don't want to believe me, then ask my 
ex-girlfriend yourself. She's a student here.

11:06.140 --> 11:07.990
I'm sure you know her too.

11:09.220 --> 11:11.270
So your ex-girlfriend is...?

11:11.600 --> 11:13.810
<b><b>Chocolate Bananas</b></b>

11:11.600 --> 11:13.810
<b>Candied Apples</b>

11:11.600 --> 11:13.810
<b>Drinks</b>

11:12.690 --> 11:15.480
Hey there. Wipe off that gloomy face.

11:15.480 --> 11:18.760
It's the cultural festival. 
Let's try to enjoy it!

11:19.440 --> 11:23.490
Yamana Nicole. 
She's Shirakawa Runa's best friend, right?

11:23.490 --> 11:26.670
Huh? You're Yamana-san's ex-boyfriend?

11:26.670 --> 11:30.210
What? Wait, the one she dated 
for just two weeks?

11:30.210 --> 11:31.420
Yeah.

11:31.420 --> 11:35.170
The one who listened to sutras 
on earphones? The super angsty one?

11:35.170 --> 11:37.020
Hey, not so loud!

11:37.020 --> 11:38.920
I already told you that it's me!

11:38.920 --> 11:44.390
<b>Maid Café</b>

11:39.240 --> 11:41.810
So why were you meeting with Runa?

11:41.810 --> 11:44.390
Well, at first, it was a coincidence.

11:44.780 --> 11:48.060
When I was on my way to cram school, 
somebody called out to me.

11:48.060 --> 11:52.870
She said, "I'm Yamana Nicole's friend.
 I want to talk to you."

11:54.140 --> 11:58.010
But I had a meeting that day 
and didn't have time.

11:58.010 --> 11:59.440
When I said no,

11:59.990 --> 12:05.560
she forced me to take her number 
and said to please call her anytime.

12:05.560 --> 12:10.750
She was pushy and also pretty cute.
Normally, you can't turn a girl like that down.

12:11.020 --> 12:12.710
Normally?

12:14.840 --> 12:16.830
Yeah. Well, anyway,

12:16.830 --> 12:20.050
I was the guy on the phone with her.

12:20.510 --> 12:24.410
After that, she got really intense 
talking about Yamana

12:24.410 --> 12:27.510
and said she wanted me to meet her 
as a surprise or something.

12:28.340 --> 12:32.430
Even though that was over
 a long time ago for me.

12:32.880 --> 12:38.400
But Yamana-san still says that she 
never stopped thinking about you.

12:38.400 --> 12:39.900
So will you?

12:39.900 --> 12:42.090
There's no way I can see her.

12:42.090 --> 12:45.440
I dumped her so I could 
fool around with other girls.

12:45.440 --> 12:49.920
After playing around so much, I just stroll 
back and say, "Actually, you were the one"?

12:49.920 --> 12:52.680
That's kind of asking a lot at this point.

12:53.480 --> 12:56.440
I know I really hurt Yamana.

12:57.330 --> 13:03.550
<b>Maid Café</b>

12:57.830 --> 13:02.660
She liked me when I was still a dork. 
She was the only girl who did.

13:03.550 --> 13:07.010
Yamana used to be pretty strait-laced, too.

13:07.400 --> 13:11.510
She was manager of the ping pong club. 
She had black hair and acted mature.

13:11.930 --> 13:16.060
She became the way she is now 
after we broke up.

13:16.600 --> 13:20.230
It was right when her parents 
were going through a rough divorce.

13:21.020 --> 13:26.970
I didn't do a thing to support her. And then 
I dumped her with some garbage excuse.

13:27.360 --> 13:31.450
<b>Maid Café</b>

13:27.710 --> 13:30.150
So you don't think you can face her now?

13:31.450 --> 13:36.250
I think you're right 
that you might have hurt her.

13:37.000 --> 13:38.020
But still...

13:39.610 --> 13:45.150
there must be a way to forgive those wounds, 
forgive those mistakes, forgive the past,

13:45.150 --> 13:47.430
and keep moving forward.

13:48.820 --> 13:52.390
If you still have feelings for 
each other, now is the time.

13:52.750 --> 13:57.480
I want you to see Yamana-san one more time.

13:59.330 --> 14:00.940
I give up.

14:01.520 --> 14:05.530
Who knew you were such a love guru?

14:05.530 --> 14:06.440
Huh?

14:06.440 --> 14:08.900
I'm not like that at all...

14:08.900 --> 14:10.620
There he is! Kasshi!

14:11.720 --> 14:14.750
We asked Tanikita-san, 
and she said you might be here.

14:14.750 --> 14:16.480
What happened?

14:16.480 --> 14:20.090
You gotta come with us now! 
It's Shirakawa-san and the demon gyaru!

14:22.420 --> 14:25.920
What are you doing? 
Sekiya-san, please come with me!

14:26.200 --> 14:28.790
Huh? Uh, okay.

14:29.890 --> 14:32.350
<i>Photos for Sale</i>

14:30.010 --> 14:32.350
<i>Yakisoba</i>

14:31.590 --> 14:35.310
Oh, come on! It's totally fine.
 Really, really!

14:35.310 --> 14:38.020
And I'm telling you it's not!

14:38.020 --> 14:38.330
<b>Candied Apples</b>

14:38.020 --> 14:45.480
<b>Chocolate Bananas</b>

14:38.300 --> 14:41.230
And I'm telling you
 you're really, really cute.

14:41.230 --> 14:43.280
If you don't kiss me, I'm gonna die.

14:43.280 --> 14:45.480
Huh? Then go and die!

14:45.800 --> 14:47.860
Yes, ma'am. One "go die" for the house.

14:47.860 --> 14:49.370
Let's go, Runa.

14:49.370 --> 14:50.250
Yeah.

14:51.440 --> 14:54.780
Yeah! Totally awesome defense!

14:56.660 --> 14:57.620
Runa!

15:00.460 --> 15:01.850
Ryuto?

15:02.420 --> 15:05.370
Eww, serious? Boyfriend to the rescue?

15:05.370 --> 15:07.380
Wow, what a cool dude.

15:09.340 --> 15:10.810
L-Let's go.

15:11.610 --> 15:12.790
But...

15:14.290 --> 15:14.850
Okay!

15:14.850 --> 15:19.980
<b>Chocolate Bananas</b>

15:14.850 --> 15:19.980
<b>Candied Apples</b>

15:14.850 --> 15:19.980
<b><i>Yakisoba</i></b>

15:15.130 --> 15:18.220
So Miss Friend here is gonna 
give us that kiss instead.

15:18.220 --> 15:19.980
Huh?! Go to hell!

15:20.250 --> 15:21.800
And then?

15:22.780 --> 15:25.900
Back off. That's my girlfriend.

15:25.900 --> 15:27.360
Uh...

15:30.200 --> 15:31.430
Sorry, man.

15:35.200 --> 15:37.110
Come on. We're going.

15:38.800 --> 15:40.860
Senpai...?

15:43.750 --> 15:44.920
But how...?

15:46.760 --> 15:48.840
Sorry I took so long.

16:05.370 --> 16:07.730
We're happy for you, Yamana-san.

16:08.280 --> 16:11.210
I can't compete with that. It's a losing game.

16:11.210 --> 16:13.980
Why does the sutra guy get the demon gyaru?

16:13.980 --> 16:16.570
Ah, I want to be in love.

16:17.100 --> 16:21.620
Okay, I'm doing it. I'm confessing 
my feelings to Tanikita-san!

16:23.080 --> 16:25.040
Huh?!

16:26.870 --> 16:30.420
I-I like you! Please go out with me!

16:42.670 --> 16:44.080
Ijichi-kun.

16:44.080 --> 16:45.690
Y-Yes?

16:46.250 --> 16:49.020
This is what you call unwanted advances.

16:49.020 --> 16:50.010
Huh?

16:51.290 --> 16:54.840
I don't know anything 
about you yet, Ijichi-kun.

16:54.840 --> 16:57.700
What made you think I'd say yes?

16:57.700 --> 16:59.910
Uh, um, uh...

16:59.910 --> 17:03.000
Do you actually like me, Ijichi-kun?

17:03.000 --> 17:05.640
Why? Since when? What started it?

17:05.640 --> 17:07.510
What part? My looks?

17:07.510 --> 17:11.830
If that's it, then am I supposed to 
like you for your looks, too?

17:13.610 --> 17:19.400
A confession should be something people do 
to confirm their feelings for each other.

17:19.400 --> 17:22.140
It isn't something you just take 
a random chance on!

17:23.640 --> 17:27.850
Sure, it hurts to get turned down, 
but it also hurts to turn someone down

17:27.850 --> 17:32.030
because you know it's going to destroy 
the person standing right in front of you!

17:33.850 --> 17:36.250
Confessing your feelings isn't a game!

17:36.250 --> 17:41.620
Isn't love more about trying <i>not</i> to 
force your feelings on someone you like?

17:50.720 --> 17:52.340
I'm sorry, Ijichi-kun.

17:52.900 --> 17:56.160
Akari is really cute, but she's always single,

17:56.160 --> 17:58.490
so boys ask her out all the time.

17:58.490 --> 18:00.650
And each time, she gets depressed and says,

18:01.350 --> 18:06.660
"It might have gone differently if 
we'd become better friends first."

18:07.270 --> 18:13.340
She's super serious about dating 
and falling in love and stuff.

18:13.340 --> 18:14.480
So I hope...

18:16.630 --> 18:18.410
you can respect that.

18:24.760 --> 18:27.470
We're failing at the game of youth.

18:27.470 --> 18:29.660
At least you got to ask her out, though.

18:29.660 --> 18:33.930
I already lost to the angsty cool dude 
who listened to Buddhist sutras.

18:34.350 --> 18:36.620
I mean, I couldn't even compete.

18:37.420 --> 18:40.260
You're amazing, Kasshi. Seriously.

18:40.260 --> 18:41.020
Huh?

18:41.500 --> 18:46.380
You liked someone, and then 
she started to like you back...

18:46.380 --> 18:48.020
It's some kind of miracle.

18:48.850 --> 18:50.780
Yeah, seriously.

18:50.780 --> 18:55.070
Kasshi didn't fail. 
He's a guiding star of hope for us geeks.

18:55.070 --> 18:57.280
I don't know...

18:57.710 --> 19:01.490
Is it really okay for us 
to keep dating like this?

19:02.360 --> 19:04.070
Of course it's okay.

19:04.450 --> 19:05.710
Huh?

19:05.710 --> 19:06.910
Kasshi?

19:06.910 --> 19:09.850
Sorry! I need to go look for Runa.

19:11.810 --> 19:13.520
Good luck, comrade!

19:13.520 --> 19:16.010
Capture the happiness that escaped us!

19:16.840 --> 19:18.800
<b>Seirin Festival</b>

19:18.800 --> 19:20.760
<b>Seirin Festival</b>

19:26.930 --> 19:29.420
So in your class, Maririn...

19:38.480 --> 19:39.540
Runa!

19:43.450 --> 19:45.110
Not here either?

19:49.690 --> 19:50.840
Ryuto.

19:51.690 --> 19:52.790
Runa!

19:56.750 --> 19:59.210
<b>Seirin Festival</b>

19:57.920 --> 20:02.000
I had no idea that you knew Sekiya-san.

20:02.000 --> 20:04.380
Yeah, we go to the same cram school.

20:04.380 --> 20:09.590
I knew what he looked like because Nicole 
showed me one of her old pictures.

20:10.250 --> 20:13.900
That day, I randomly saw 
someone who looked like him,

20:13.900 --> 20:16.360
and decided to ask and find out.

20:16.360 --> 20:18.940
I knew it was a chance I couldn't pass up.

20:20.320 --> 20:22.200
No kidding.

20:24.110 --> 20:26.990
And you thought I had a sugar daddy?

20:27.520 --> 20:30.450
No. No, I didn't.

20:30.860 --> 20:35.020
Akari told me. She got the wrong idea 
and then blabbed it all to you.

20:35.020 --> 20:36.080
Yeah.

20:36.080 --> 20:39.870
That expensive bag is something 
my grandma gave me.

20:39.870 --> 20:43.030
She said that kind of design is 
more flattering for young girls.

20:44.000 --> 20:49.020
But thanks to that misunderstanding, 
Nicole was able to see Sekiya-san again.

20:49.820 --> 20:52.350
Thank you, Ryuto.

20:52.350 --> 20:55.810
But... I don't deserve any credit.

20:55.810 --> 20:59.880
It's all because you had the courage 
to talk to Sekiya-san.

21:02.770 --> 21:05.110
The whole Nicole thing got me thinking.

21:05.620 --> 21:09.080
If you like each other, 
you should be together, right?

21:09.520 --> 21:10.520
Yeah.

21:11.420 --> 21:15.670
Life is short. If you avoid 
the person you like...

21:16.130 --> 21:18.000
What a waste of youth.

21:18.380 --> 21:20.630
I think... so, too.

21:25.350 --> 21:30.810
Maybe life does seem short, 
but I bet it's actually pretty long.

21:31.270 --> 21:32.560
What do you mean?

21:32.560 --> 21:36.270
There's still next year, the next year, 
and all the years after that.

21:36.680 --> 21:42.830
I want to spend all that time 
with you, Runa. I really do.

23:26.830 --> 23:28.600
On the next <i>Our Dating Story</i>,

23:28.600 --> 23:32.010
the experienced you and the inexperienced me

23:32.010 --> 23:33.890
break up.

23:34.290 --> 23:37.930
I feel Runa's feelings
so much right now.

23:37.930 --> 23:39.930
<b>Our Breakup Story: The Experienced You and the Inexperienced Me Break Up.</b>
